  "findings": {
    "best_full_sample": "F_Vol_Adjusted",
    "best_oos_avg": "A_Static_GLD",
    "best_oos_sharpe": 1.1181,
    "significant_improvements_vs_gld": [],
    "harvey_pass": false
  },
  "conclusion": "No dynamic safe-allocation strategy significantly outperforms static GLD at Harvey t>3.0 threshold. Best OOS: A_Static_GLD (Sharpe=1.1181). In fact, TLT (t=-4.60) and Momentum switching (t=-4.56) are significantly WORSE than static GLD, confirming GLD dominance. Vol-adjusted (F) has highest full-sample Sharpe (0.897) but fails OOS due to TLT drag in 2022. The key insight: GLD wins in high-rate and rising-rate regimes where TLT collapses, and these regimes dominate the recent period (2022-2026). During low-rate periods (<2%), TLT actually beats GLD (Sharpe 1.24 vs 0.70), but you cannot predict rate regimes in advance with sufficient accuracy. Recommendation: maintain 50/50 SPY/GLD + 12/VIX framework. Extends K507, N176, T19, K425.",
  "references": [
    "Moreira & Muir (2017), Volatility-Managed Portfolios, JoF 72(4):1611-1644",
    "Baele et al. (2010), Flights to Safety, RFS",
    "Campbell, Sunderam, Viceira (2017), Inflation Bets or Deflation Hedges?, JoF 72(4):1645-1692",
    "Prior experiments: T19 (TLT structural break), K425 (bond-equity decorrelation), K507 (dynamic SPY-GLD), N176 (conditional TLT)"
  ]
